                <pb facs="0405" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123W451/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-07T16:00:00-04:00">July 7, 1933—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Personal for the Ambassador. Could you give me any idea how much longer you
                    feel that, in justice to the work which you are now doing, you should remain in
                    Habana? I realize, of course, that there is still much to be done in the
                    political field, as well as in the negotiations for the revision of the
                    commercial treaty. With me it is a question of considering whether it would be
                    worth while to appoint Caffery Assistant Secretary of State pending your
                    return.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
